"outside the sparse specification relative to when the operation began, BUT "
"these commands often make a commit just before or after such that by the end "
"of the operation there is no change to the index outside the sparse "
"specification.  Of course, if the operation hits conflicts or does not make "
"a commit, then these operations clearly can modify the index outside the "
"sparse specification."
