#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:946
msgid ""
"This list used to be a lot longer (see e.g. [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9]), but we've "
"been working on it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:950
msgid ""
"Behavior A is not well supported in Git.  (Behavior B didn't used to be "
"either, but was the easier of the two to implement.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:952
msgid "am and apply:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:958
msgid ""
"apply, without `--index` or `--cached`, relies on files being present in the "
"working copy, and also writes to them unconditionally.  As such, it should "
"first check for the files' presence, and if found to be SKIP_WORKTREE, then "
"clear the bit and vivify the paths, then do its work.  Currently, it just "
"throws an error."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:963
msgid ""
"apply, with either `--cached` or `--index`, will not preserve the "
"SKIP_WORKTREE bit.  This is fine if the file has conflicts, but otherwise "
"SKIP_WORKTREE bits should be preserved for --cached and probably also for "
"--index."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:970
msgid ""
"am, if there are no conflicts, will vivify files and fail to preserve the "
"SKIP_WORKTREE bit.  If there are conflicts and `-3` is not specified, it "
"will vivify files and then complain the patch doesn't apply.  If there are "
"conflicts and `-3` is specified, it will vivify files and then complain that "
"those vivified files would be overwritten by merge."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:972
msgid "reset --hard:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:975
msgid ""
"reset --hard provides confusing error message (works correctly, but misleads "
"the user into believing it didn't):"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:991
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ touch addme\n"
"$ git add addme\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H addme\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git reset --hard                           # usually works great\n"
"error: Path 'addme' not uptodate; will not remove from working tree.\n"
"HEAD is now at bdbbb6f third\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ ls -1\n"
"tracked\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:995
msgid ""
"`git reset --hard` DID remove addme from the index and the working tree, "
"contrary to the error message, but in line with how reset --hard should "
"behave."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1001
msgid ""
"`read-tree` doesn't apply the 'SKIP_WORKTREE' bit to *any* of the entries it "
"reads into the index, resulting in all your files suddenly appearing to be "
"\"deleted\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1003
msgid "Checkout, restore:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1005
msgid "These command do not handle path & revision arguments appropriately:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1031
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ ls\n"
"tracked\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"S tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$ git checkout -- '*skipped'\n"
"error: pathspec '*skipped' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git ls-files -- '*skipped'\n"
"tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD -- '*skipped'\n"
"error: pathspec '*skipped' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git ls-tree HEAD | grep skipped\n"
"100644 blob "
"276f5a64354b791b13840f02047738c77ad0584f\ttracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD~1 -- '*skipped'\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"H tracked\n"
"H tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"M  tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD -- '*skipped'\n"
"$ git status --porcelain\n"
"$\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1036
msgid ""
"Note that checkout without a revision (or restore --staged) fails to find a "
"file to restore from the index, even though ls-files shows such a file "
"certainly exists."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1040
msgid ""
"Similar issues occur with HEAD (--source=HEAD in restore's case), but "
"suddenly works when HEAD~1 is specified.  And then after that it will work "
"with HEAD specified, even though it didn't before."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1042
msgid "Directories are also an issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1048
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ git sparse-checkout set nomatches\n"
"$ git status\n"
"On branch main\n"
"You are in a sparse checkout with 0% of tracked files present.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1057
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"nothing to commit, working tree clean\n"
"$ git checkout .\n"
"error: pathspec '.' did not match any file(s) known to git\n"
"$ git checkout HEAD~1 .\n"
"Updated 1 path from 58916d9\n"
"$ git ls-files -t\n"
"S tracked\n"
"H tracked-but-maybe-skipped\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1060
msgid "checkout and restore --staged, continued:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/technical/sparse-checkout.txt:1064
msgid ""
"These commands do not correctly scope operations to the sparse "
"specification, and make it worse by not setting important SKIP_WORKTREE "
